Package: amber-glycin
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, bubblewrap, amber-gtk4 (>= 4.16.13)
Description: glycin image-loading runtime bundle for the amber suite
 One glycin build shared by the amber applications, installed to
 /usr/lib/amber-glycin and reached only through those applications'
 RUNPATH. It is deliberately not on the ldconfig path, so installing it
 cannot change what anything else on the system links against.
 .
 glycin decodes images in sandboxed loader processes (bubblewrap and
 seccomp) and hands the pixels back through a memfd. The package holds
 libglycin-2, libglycin-gtk4-2, and the 2+ loaders with their config.
 Linux Mint ships only the 1+ loaders and no libglycin. Applications set
 GLYCIN_DATA_DIR to /usr/lib/amber-glycin/share before the first load.

Package: amber-glycin-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: amd64
Depends: amber-glycin (= ${binary:Version}), amber-gtk4-dev (>= 4.16.13), libglib2.0-dev, libfontconfig-dev, libseccomp-dev
Description: glycin development files for the amber suite's bundle
 The headers, pkg-config files and unversioned library links of the
 amber-glycin bundle (libglycin-2 and libglycin-gtk4-2), all under
 /usr/lib/amber-glycin. The suite's Odin binding is generated from these
 headers.
 .
 Build with PKG_CONFIG_PATH set to
 /usr/lib/amber-glycin/pkgconfig:/usr/lib/amber-gtk4/pkgconfig, give the
 program the RUNPATH /usr/lib/amber-glycin:/usr/lib/amber-gtk4, and set
 GLYCIN_DATA_DIR to /usr/lib/amber-glycin/share before the first load.
